        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree, that button shouldn't even be there. \"Cancel immediately\" sounds like you want to end a subscription, not that you want to give up what you won't get refunded. \n\nAlthough removing a subscription earlier voluntarily can make sense in some rare cases, it's definitely not the standard use case, so it should not be disguised as a harmless cancel button in default color. It should be red, with a big red warning that clarifies that you won't get your money back and give up the rewards that you already paid for if you click it.\n\nI have at least one customer who probably ran into this trap and wanted to cancel the refundable part of the subscription, but cancelled it immediately instead.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
